Z||000002||Richard Parnell||12-10-1999||03:50 PM||||Thanks Phil.  Now there is still the debate over the issue of whether the Isuzu and Getrag can handle the installation of a V8.  In discussions with many different people such as Batman , V8 Archie, and companies (Ace and others) some people insist the Getrag and Isuzu will not handle the power and others say no problem.  V8 Archie insists that he has had no failures with his kits.  I really want to do the V8 conversion using a 4 barrel.  I want to get totally away from the computerized aspects of the car.  The computer will only run the dashboard lights eventually.  I have the engine but am still working on other parts like suspension, radiator, etc. But I guess I should just go ahead and do the switch and see what happens.  I'm so tired of guys in their Mustangs and Irocs giving me grief going down the road.||||reg||5
Z||000003||four50four||12-10-1999||04:35 PM||||isn't the 5-speed getrag almost bulletproof, or is that the 4 speed muncie...||||reg||1
Z||000005||william_thorniii||12-10-1999||07:57 PM||||I wouldn't necessarily trust someone selling a product.  Although I have heard many good stories about V-8 Archie, I have heard as many horror stories.  Rodney Dickman is know to many Fieroites as "The Getrag Guy".  I can guarantee that any information provided by him is as accurate as far as he knows.  He might have a better feel for what they can reliably endure.  For the record, I have always been under the impression that the 4-spd was the trans. to go with for a V-8.  Especially since the gearing is better for straight line runs and with the added weight (I know, I know... its only 160+ pounds, but for you straight line guys that is over .1s) you probably aren't interested in road race applications.  But that is just my $.02<P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||1
Z||000006||batboy||12-10-1999||11:24 PM||||I don't remember ever knocking the Getrag or saying that it won't hold up. I have said that ANY of the Fiero trannies will probably break if you thrashed and abuse them too many times with a V8 or any other high torque engine.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Richard Parnell||12-11-1999||08:51 PM||||Sorry Batboy, I sure didn't mean to say you were badmouthing the tranny.  I meant some other people I've spoken to.||||reg||11
Z||000008||rcn491||12-13-1999||08:38 PM||||For a V8 conversion you might consider adding the reinforcement bearings. They replace the existing oil seals and can be added just by pulling the drive shafts.<BR>||||reg||1
